  "summary": "BabLock is a ransomware family targeting Windows, Linux, and ESXi systems, first observed in mid-2022. The sophisticated Windows version employs DLL side-loading, process injection, and GPO modification for lateral movement, while the Linux/ESXi variants are based on the leaked Babuk source code. The group operates stealthily, forgoing a public data leak site and using email for communication.",
